    "https://jobs.ufl.edu/career-growth/career-paths/": {
      "title": "Career Paths",
      "description": "Career Paths - Careers Skip to content Main Navigation Careers Benefits Benefits Plans Time-Away Perks & Support Community The University of Florida Working at UF Career Growth ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Paths Career Types Resources How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference Explore Jobs How can we help you? Homepage Career Growth Career Paths Career Paths Benefits Benefits Plans Time-Away Perks & Support Community The University of Florida Working at UF Career Growth ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Paths Career Types Resources How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference How to Qualify for Veterans’ Preference Resources for Veterans Explore Jobs At the University of Florida, there are many different ways to develop your career. Some of these include networking at various workshops, advancing your degree through the UF Employee Education Program, and expanding your working knowledge through many training programs. The path to career progression is not always linear but is unique to each individual employee. In addition, the direction of one’s career development is dependent on various factors, such as one’s passion, motivation, work history/experience and understanding of the potential pathways. Potential Career Pathways Each position at the University of Florida is uniquely designed to meet the requirements and the demands of the hiring managers throughout the campus; however, many positions share some requirements — knowledge, skills, abilities and competencies — that would allow a person to progress from one classification series (e.g. administrative support assistant) to another series (e.g. fiscal assistant). Given the nature of the complexity of mapping out all possible career paths for each position at the University of Florida, the maps below reflect the common pathways for all staff positions within its job family.  For more information on these job family, please visit the TEAMS Titles website. Accounting & Finance Accounting & Finance Accounting and finance positions play pivotal roles in managing the financial health and operations of organizations. Accountants focus on recording, analyzing, and reporting financial transactions, ensuring accuracy and compliance with regulations. Meanwhile, finance professionals handle strategic financial planning, investment analysis, risk management, and capital allocation to support organizational growth and profitability. Unique Competencies BUDGET MANAGEMENT BUSINESS MATH E-PROCUREMENT FINANCIAL & ACCOUNTING SYSTEMS FINANCIAL ANALYSIS FINANCIAL REPORTING MANAGING EXPENSES & FINANCES PROBLEM SOLVING Administration & Management Administration & Management Administration and management positions require a diverse set of competencies to effectively oversee operations, lead teams and drive organizational success. Unique Competencies ACCOUNTABILITY COLLABORATION EFFECTIVE COMMUNICATION EMOTIONAL INTELLIGENCE LEADERSHIP PROBLEM SOLVING RISK MANAGEMENT STRATEGIC THINKING Advancement Advancement Professionals in these roles cultivate and steward relationships with alumni, donors, corporations, and foundations to garner financial contributions that advance institutional priorities, such as scholarships, research initiatives, and infrastructure development. They devise strategic fundraising campaigns, engage in donor prospecting, and orchestrate donor recognition programs to build a robust culture of giving within the university community. Unique Competencies ACCOUNTABILITY ADAPTABILITY/INNOVATION COLLABORATION CREDIBILITY CRITICAL THINKING DONOR FOCUS EFFECTIVE COMMUNICATION ENGAGING COMMUNICATION ENTREPRENEURIAL SPIRIT MANAGES EXECUTION MISSION DRIVEN ORGANIZATIONAL ACUMEN RELATIONSHIP MASTERY STAKEHOLDER FOCUS STRATEGIC THINKING TENACITY Agricultural & IFAS Operations Agricultural & IFAS Operations This job family encompasses roles essential for the management and execution of agricultural activities, research, and extension programs. Animal & Veterinary Care Animal & Veterinary Care This job family encompasses a wide range of roles dedicated to the health, welfare, and treatment of animals across various settings, including veterinary hospitals, research facilities, and animal care operations. Communications, Sales & Marketing Communications, Sales & Marketing Professionals in communication, sales, and marketing are communications professionals, media relations experts, content creators, designers, event planners, broadcast and news managers, videographers and social media strategists who collaborate to effectively advance the university’s reputation locally, nationally and internationally. Unique Competencies CONTENT EVALUATION COPYWRITING AND EDITING CREATIVITY EVENT MANAGEMENT EXECUTION FACILITATIVE DECISION MAKING FAIR AND LEGAL MANAGEMENT MULTIMEDIA TOOLS NEWS MEDIA COMMUNICATIONS POLITICAL SAVVY STRATEGIC THINKING TEAMWORK Education & Training Education & Training Professionals in these roles design, implement, and evaluate educational programs, curriculum, and training initiatives to equip individuals with the knowledge, skills, and competencies needed to succeed in their fields. They employ diverse instructional methods, technology, and assessment tools to facilitate effective learning experiences. Education and training professionals also stay abreast of emerging trends, research, and best practices to continuously enhance the quality and relevance of educational offerings. Unique Competencies CURRICULUM DESIGN EDUCATIONAL PSYCHOLOGY EFFECTIVE PRESENTATIONS EMOTIONAL INTELLIGENCE PLANNING & ORGANIZING TRAINING & DEVELOPMENT Facilities Operations Facilities Operations This job family encompasses a wide range of roles responsible for the maintenance, management and operation of physical infrastructure and facilities. Health Care Health Care This job family encompasses a wide range of roles dedicated to promoting, maintaining and restoring health in individuals and communities. Human Resources Human Resources Professionals in human resources focus on the employee experience, from recruitment to retirement and everything in between. HR functions include talent acquisition, administration, compensation, benefits, training and development, employee relations, and performance management. Unique Competencies ACCURACY & ATTENTION TO DETAIL CONFIDENTIALITY HR LEGAL & REGULATORY ENVIRONMENT HUMAN RESOURCE CONSULTING HUMAN RESOURCES POLICIES, STRATEGIES & ENVIRONMENT INTERPERSONAL RELATIONSHIPS KNOWLEDGE OF ORGANIZATION SERVICE EXCELLENCE Information Technology Information Technology Information technology (IT) positions require a unique blend of technical expertise, problem-solving skills, and strategic thinking to effectively manage and innovate within the digital landscape. Unique Competencies CAPACITY PLANNING & MANAGEMENT CORE APPLICATION SYSTEMS IT STANDARDS, PROCEDURES & POLICIES PRODUCING RESULTS PRODUCTS & SERVICES REQUIREMENTS ANALYSIS TECHNICAL TROUBLESHOOTING WORKFLOW ANALYSIS Compliance, Legal & Audit Services Compliance, Legal & Audit Services This job family is comprised of professionals dedicated to ensuring adherence to regulatory requirements, mitigating risks and safeguarding organizational integrity. Libraries & Museums Libraries & Museums This job family is comprised of professionals dedicated to the preservation, curation, and management of cultural and historical artifacts for public access and education. Life, Physical & Social Sciences Life, Physical & Social Sciences This job family encompass a wide range of roles that contribute to research, experimentation, and discovery across various fields. Unique Competencies ACCURACY AND ATTENTION TO DETAIL EMPLOYEE HEALTH AND SAFETY LABORATORY EQUIPMENT OPERATION PROBLEM SOLVING RESEARCH ANALYSIS RESEARCH AND DEVELOPMENT FUNCTION Office & Business Administration Office & Business Administration Professionals in office and business administration manage, perform and/or assist with a variety of administrative tasks, operations, and finance maintenance in support of the organization’s function(s) while organizing unit’s data and maintaining quality customer service values. Unique Competencies CALENDARING CUSTOMER SUPPORT POLICIES, STANDARDS AND PROCEDURES FINANCIAL RECORD KEEPING MANAGING MULTIPLE PRIORITIES OFFICE ADMINISTRATION PROCESS MANAGEMENT QUALITY MANAGEMENT SERVICE REQUEST MANAGEMENT PROCESS (TCS) Public & Environmental Safety Public & Environmental Safety This job family is comprised of professionals dedicated to safeguarding individuals, communities and the environment through proactive safety measures and response protocols. Research & Grants Research & Grants This job family encompasses a wide array of roles crucial for supporting and advancing research initiatives and securing funding opportunities within academic, scientific and institutional settings. Student & Academic Services Student & Academic Services Professionals in student and academic services cultivate meaningful experiences and initiatives that support student well-being, campus organizations and communities, career design, and academic success. Unique Competencies EVENT MANAGEMENT FINANCIAL AID PROGRAMS AND POLICIES PROJECT MANAGEMENT RISK MANAGEMENT SERVICE EXCELLENCE STUDENT ADMISSIONS STUDENT COUNSELING STUDENT ORIENTATION STUDENT REGISTRATION For a full listing of competencies Please visit our Job Competency Library to explore competency definitions, behavior statements, interview questions and associated TEAMS Titles. Job Competency Library It is important to note that: These maps do not promise or provide any guarantee that you will automatically move into the next job. It is just the common pathway. Positions placed in the “stand alone” box on each map do not mean that there is no career progression available. It may mean that the path will cross into another job family. These maps only reflect the progression for all staff positions that are found on UF OnTarget site. Employees in USPS positions that are not listed on the UF OnTarget site can contact Classification and Compensation to determine the equivalent position and appropriate career progression map listed here. For the health care job family, due to the nature of the partnership between UF and Shands, some career progression paths may cross over to Shands Hospital. Career progression paths can evolve through time as a result of various factors, including change in the nature of the position and demands of job requirements. For questions or additional information regarding these maps, please contact Classification & Compensation . Take the next step toward your career goals. Explore a wide variety of unique opportunities at the University of Florida. Explore Jobs Popular Topics How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference Benefits Plans Career Paths Perks & Support Career Types Time-Away Working at UF The University of Florida ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Growth About UF About the University of Florida Our Research & Impact Learn about UF’s benefits Worklife Resources Connect Talent Acquisition & Onboarding 8am-5pm (352) 392-2477 talent@hr.ufl.edu 903 West University Avenue Gainesville, FL 32601 Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Privacy Statement Google Analytics Privacy Policy Translate Text-Only Site Map Web Update Requests Copyright © 2026, University of Florida"
    },
    "https://jobs.ufl.edu/career-growth/career-types/": {
      "title": "Career Types",
      "description": "Career Types - Careers Skip to content Main Navigation Careers Benefits Benefits Plans Time-Away Perks & Support Community The University of Florida Working at UF Career Growth ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Paths Career Types Resources How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference Explore Jobs How can we help you? Homepage Career Growth Career Types Career Types Benefits Benefits Plans Time-Away Perks & Support Community The University of Florida Working at UF Career Growth ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Paths Career Types Resources How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference How to Qualify for Veterans’ Preference Resources for Veterans Explore Jobs Faculty Join a community of distinguished scholars and educators at the University of Florida, where your expertise will drive innovation, teaching and research excellence. Here, faculty members are empowered with comprehensive support and opportunities for career advancement, contributing to our dynamic academic environment. Adjunct Faculty Temporary faculty positions for the purpose of temporary teaching, research, or extension functions in connection with established programs. Faculty Administrative Title Faculty positions designating appointment to an administrative role in addition to the regular faculty appointment. Multi-Track Faculty Faculty positions that can be filled either as tenure-track or non-tenure-track, depending on the selected candidate’s qualifications. Non-Permanent Status Faculty Faculty positions that formerly qualified for permanent status or are restricted by modifiers. Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Faculty positions having the principal responsibility of only teaching, research or service. Positions are not eligible for award of tenure. Permanent Status Faculty Faculty positions for limited use only; status is similar to tenure (continual appointment), once earned. Titles are not eligible if they include the following modifiers: adjunct, provisional, visiting, research, program or courtesy. Tenure-Track Faculty Faculty positions having the principal responsibilities of teaching, research, and service, directly related to the academic mission and accomplishment of the University goals. Positions are eligible for award of tenure when specific conditions have been met, and they generally require the highest degree granted in the relevant field. Visiting Faculty Faculty positions that are available for limited periods of time. Staff Join our community of career professionals in a variety of roles across a range of fields such as accounting, IT, health care, and more, and contribute to a thriving environment that values innovation, excellence, and professional growth. Whether you’re seeking full-time, part-time, or temporary positions, we offer opportunities for career advancement and skill development in a supportive and inclusive workplace. Staff Full-Time or Part-Time (TEAMS) Technical, Executive, Administrative and Managerial Support. The University of Florida offers Full-Time or Part-Time Staff positions classified as TEAMS. The TEAMS classification can be permanent or time-limited for hourly or salary positions. Staff positions range from Mechanics, HR Assistant, Custodial Workers, Finance Analyst, and Research Coordinators to Director and Assistant Vice Presidents. Additional information about Staff-Full Time / Part-Time (TEAMS) employment can be found in our Employee Handbook. Temporary Full-Time or Part-Time (OPS) OPS, or “Other Personnel Services” temporary employment comprises the University of Florida’s at-will, temporary jobs. OPS temporary appointments can be terminated at any time without cause. Please note that OPS temporary appointments are distinct from time-limited Staff Full-Time positions. It is at the hiring department’s discretion to prolong an OPS temporary appointment. In fact, in some cases an OPS appointment can last several years depending on the funding. Time Limited Positions Time limited positions are based on circumstances, such as funding sources, which control the length of time for which the position is available. A time-limited position shall have the same rights as a position with a regular appointment modifier, except such position does not have rights provided for layoff, recall, and notice of non-reappointment. Other Opportunities Graduate Assistants Join us as a Graduate Assistant at the University of Florida and make a significant impact on teaching and research while advancing your own graduate education. Enjoy a biweekly paycheck, in-state tuition, and health insurance, all while gaining invaluable professional experience and putting classroom theory into practice. Student Assistants Student Assistants include undergraduate and graduate students. A Student Assistant is a person enrolled at the University of Florida in a degree program and is being employed in a department performing non-academic work, which differentiates their classification from that of a graduate assistant. Postdoctoral Associate Elevate your research career as a Postdoctoral Scholar at the University of Florida, where you’ll collaborate on groundbreaking projects, receive a competitive salary, and enjoy comprehensive benefits, all while advancing your professional expertise. Join a future-forward community dedicated to innovation and academic excellence. This is a temporary academic appointment requiring a doctorate in an appropriate field; appointment may last up to four years. Often used for research-related roles. Take the next step toward your career goals. Explore a wide variety of unique opportunities at the University of Florida. Explore Jobs Page Contents Popular Topics How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference Benefits Plans Career Paths Perks & Support Career Types Time-Away Working at UF The University of Florida ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Growth About UF About the University of Florida Our Research & Impact Learn about UF’s benefits Worklife Resources Connect Talent Acquisition & Onboarding 8am-5pm (352) 392-2477 talent@hr.ufl.edu 903 West University Avenue Gainesville, FL 32601 Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Privacy Statement Google Analytics Privacy Policy Translate Text-Only Site Map Web Update Requests Copyright © 2026, University of Florida"
    },
    "https://jobs.ufl.edu/resources/how-to-apply/": {
      "title": "How to Apply",
      "description": "How to Apply - Careers Skip to content Main Navigation Careers Benefits Benefits Plans Time-Away Perks & Support Community The University of Florida Working at UF Career Growth ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Paths Career Types Resources How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference Explore Jobs How can we help you? Homepage Resources How to Apply How to Apply Benefits Benefits Plans Time-Away Perks & Support Community The University of Florida Working at UF Career Growth ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Paths Career Types Resources How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference How to Qualify for Veterans’ Preference Resources for Veterans Explore Jobs The University of Florida offers a variety of exciting job opportunities for faculty and staff positions. All open positions are hosted with PageUp. Applications must be submitted online via the Careers at UF website and go directly to the department who makes the ultimate hiring decision. Whether you are a new or returning applicant, you may find this applicant tutorial on UF’s application system helpful. The applicant tutorial provides information on how to: Search for positions Sign up to receive positions via emails Applying for a position Managing your profile Contact information Career Development Hub At UF, we encourage career exploration, development, and success. The Career Development Hub is designed to help employees manage and navigate their career paths at UF. Career Development Hub – Make a Move You've Applied, What's Next? The recruitment process can take several weeks. The time frame varies greatly based on factors such as the volume of applicants, the department’s schedule, and the need for the job. You may log in to your account to check the status of an application at any time. Take a look at the steps below on what to expect once you’ve submitted your application. Application Submitted – Submit an online application to the position of interest. If the position is eligible for veteran’s preference, attach the DD214 to the application. Be sure to refer to the Application Instructions section of each posting for information regarding required documents, special instructions for applicants, or contact information of the hiring department. Automatic Confirmation Email – UF will send a confirmation email once the online application is received. The recruitment process timeframe varies based on the volume of applicants and the department’s needs. Contact for Interview – If a department or search committee is interested in moving forward with your application, you will be contacted to set up an interview. Outcome Notification – The department will notify all applicants the outcome of the recruitment process once a candidate has been selected for the position. Popular Topics How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference Benefits Plans Career Paths Perks & Support Career Types Time-Away Working at UF The University of Florida ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Growth About UF About the University of Florida Our Research & Impact Learn about UF’s benefits Worklife Resources Connect Talent Acquisition & Onboarding 8am-5pm (352) 392-2477 talent@hr.ufl.edu 903 West University Avenue Gainesville, FL 32601 Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Privacy Statement Google Analytics Privacy Policy Translate Text-Only Site Map Web Update Requests Copyright © 2026, University of Florida"
    },
    "https://jobs.ufl.edu/resources/frequently-asked-questions/": {
      "title": "Frequently Asked Questions",
      "description": "Frequently Asked Questions - Careers Skip to content Main Navigation Careers Benefits Benefits Plans Time-Away Perks & Support Community The University of Florida Working at UF Career Growth ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Paths Career Types Resources How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference Explore Jobs How can we help you? Homepage Resources Frequently Asked Questions Frequently Asked Questions Benefits Benefits Plans Time-Away Perks & Support Community The University of Florida Working at UF Career Growth ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Paths Career Types Resources How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference How to Qualify for Veterans’ Preference Resources for Veterans Explore Jobs Account Settings in Careers at UF How do I set up an account in the Careers at UF system? To create an account, click “Apply Now” button on the position you are interested in. You will be prompted to enter a valid email address to create an account. On the “Personal Details” section of the application, you will create a password that you will continue to use each time you log in to your account. Please use the same email address each time you apply for a position. This will assist UF in processing your application as quickly as possible. Can I update my name, email, or my address on my account? Yes, when you are logging into the applicant site, you can update your profile information by clicking on the Update profile tab on the top right-hand side of the home screen. I can't remember my password. How do I reset it? Locate the Login button at explore.jobs.ufl.edu and click the “Forgotten your password?” link. Enter the email address associated with your account and click “OK.” An email will be sent with instructions on how to reset your password. Language in Job Postings What is the time frame of a Time Limited position? (For TEAMS positions only) Time limited positions are based on circumstances, such as funding sources, which control the length of time for which the position is available. A time-limited position has the same rights as a position with a regular appointment modifier, except such position does not have rights provided for layoff and/or recall. If funding ends, the employee is given a 45-day notice period. Does UF sponsor employment visas for staff and faculty positions? Yes, the University as an institution does offer visa sponsorship; however, that is done at the discretion of each hiring department. In the event that the hiring department offers an applicant visa sponsorship additional information will be required. Most visa processes usually last 4-6 months, in some cases longer. What is the cutoff time to submit an application? Applications must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (EST) of the date listed in the Applications Close field. Prior to Submitting Your Application What are the acceptable file formats for attached documents? The supported file extensions for document uploads in the Careers at UF system are: .doc, .docx, .docm, .pdf, .txt, .rtf, .htm, .html, .msg, .dat, .csv, and .pgp. Your documents will have to be saved in one of these formats in order to upload them to your application. To whom should I address my cover letter? You do not need to address your cover letter to a particular individual unless indicated in the instructions to applicants found on the job posting. Can I upload my files, such as resume, from my Dropbox or Google Drive account? Yes. How do I upload documents to my application with Dropbox or Google Drive? Click the button for either option to sign into your account and select the file you wish to use. You may be prompted with a dialog to allow the system to access the documents in your account. Click the “Accept” button to ensure that you can upload documents into your application. What kind of documents can I upload from Dropbox or Google Drive? The supported file extensions for document uploads are: .doc, .docx, .docm, .pdf, .txt, .rtf, .htm, .html, .msg, .dat, .csv, and .pgp. Any document that has been uploaded to Google Drive and converted to a Google Doc format will be treated as a PDF. Why can't I see the Dropbox or Google Drive buttons? Please note that Dropbox and Google Drive are not supported in a number of older browsers, specifically Internet Explorer 6 and 7. Google Drive is also not available in Internet Explorer 8. Can I upload from my mobile device? From a mobile perspective, the Dropbox option is available on iOS and Android devices, but is only available on Windows Mobile devices if Internet Explorer website preferences are set to display as “desktop version.” The Google Drive option is available on iOS and Android devices, but is not available on Windows Mobile devices. Application Process How does the hiring process work? If you possess the basic qualifications for the position, as indicated by your application, your information will be reviewed by the hiring authority or search committee, as applicable. Upon the hiring authority or committee’s review of your qualifications, you may be contacted for an interview. If you successfully complete the interview process, the hiring department will check references, conduct a background check, and perform post-offer testing as required. How will I know my status on my application? The recruitment process can take several weeks. If you are selected for an interview, you will be contacted directly by the hiring department. If the position is filled or cancelled, you will receive an email notification. You will also receive a notification if you were not selected for an interview. You can check the status of your application at any time by logging in to your account and viewing your submitted application. What is the average timeframe between when a position closes and when interviews begin? The time frame varies greatly and is based on numerous factors such as the volume of applicants, the department’s schedule, the need for the job etc. Unfortunately, because of the numerous variables it is impossible to gauge how long the hiring process will take. We recommend checking the status periodically for any updates to the requisition. What does my application status mean? Under Review : the recruitment process is still underway, and your application is still being reviewed Incomplete : your application has not been completed or submitted for the position Posting Canceled: the position you applied for is no longer being recruited Withdrawn : you have removed your application for consideration Not Hired: your application is no longer under consideration for the position How can I add documents to my application, or make changes to a document that I have already uploaded to my application? Applicants should ensure all requested materials have been uploaded and attached successfully before submitting the application. Prior to the deadline of the job posting, you can choose to withdraw your application by clicking the red Withdraw button and resubmitting an application for that particular job posting. This will allow you to add or edit documents attached to your application. You will need to ensure that you resubmit your application before the application deadline, once you have edited your documents. Can I withdraw my application once I have submitted it for a specific job posting? Yes, you may withdraw your application at any time. Log in to your account and click the red button labeled Withdraw. If you would like to resubmit your application, you must do so prior to the deadline of the job posting. I made a mistake in my application. How do I correct it? Prior to the deadline of the job posting, you can choose to withdraw your application by clicking the red Withdraw button and resubmitting an application for that particular job posting. This will allow you to edit your application. You will need to ensure that you resubmit your application before the application deadline, once you have edited your application. Job Opportunities with UF Partners I'm interested in applying for a position at UF Health. How do I apply and/or check the status of my application? To apply for a UF Health position or to check your application status, please visit jobs.ufhealth.org . I'd like to apply for a food service position. How can I do this? All food service positions at UF are hired through Compass Group, and they can be reached by visiting: https://careers.compassgroupcareers.com I am interested in applying for a position with the University of Florida Athletic Association. Where do I go? Here is the link to the UAA job board and contact information: https://floridagators.com/sports/2015/12/10/_employment_.aspx Take the next step toward your career goals. Explore a wide variety of unique opportunities at the University of Florida. Explore Jobs Page Contents Popular Topics How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference Benefits Plans Career Paths Perks & Support Career Types Time-Away Working at UF The University of Florida ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Growth About UF About the University of Florida Our Research & Impact Learn about UF’s benefits Worklife Resources Connect Talent Acquisition & Onboarding 8am-5pm (352) 392-2477 talent@hr.ufl.edu 903 West University Avenue Gainesville, FL 32601 Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Privacy Statement Google Analytics Privacy Policy Translate Text-Only Site Map Web Update Requests Copyright © 2026, University of Florida"
    },
    "https://jobs.ufl.edu/resources/veterans-preference/": {
      "title": "Veterans’ Preference",
      "description": "Veterans’ Preference - Careers Skip to content Main Navigation Careers Benefits Benefits Plans Time-Away Perks & Support Community The University of Florida Working at UF Career Growth ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Paths Career Types Resources How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference Explore Jobs How can we help you? Homepage Resources Veterans’ Preference Veterans’ Preference Benefits Benefits Plans Time-Away Perks & Support Community The University of Florida Working at UF Career Growth ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Paths Career Types Resources How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference How to Qualify for Veterans’ Preference Resources for Veterans Explore Jobs Veterans’ Preference means granting the applicant further consideration than what they would have attained through their own merit. At the University of Florida we do not utilize a scoring system when reviewing applicants during the recruitment process. UF grants veteran’s preference on qualified positions with a minimum of an initial interview for all veterans who claim and are eligible for preference. An applicant who believes he or she was not afforded employment, promotion or retention preference may file a complaint with the FDVA. For more information visit Veterans’ Preference – Florida Department of Veterans’ Affairs , call (727) 518-3202, Ext. 5511 or email VeteransPreference@FDVA.FL.GOV . How to Qualify Resources for Veterans Take the next step toward your career goals. Explore a wide variety of unique opportunities at the University of Florida. Explore Jobs Page Contents Popular Topics How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference Benefits Plans Career Paths Perks & Support Career Types Time-Away Working at UF The University of Florida ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Growth About UF About the University of Florida Our Research & Impact Learn about UF’s benefits Worklife Resources Connect Talent Acquisition & Onboarding 8am-5pm (352) 392-2477 talent@hr.ufl.edu 903 West University Avenue Gainesville, FL 32601 Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Privacy Statement Google Analytics Privacy Policy Translate Text-Only Site Map Web Update Requests Copyright © 2026, University of Florida"
    },
