atalyst: Building your Professional Journey at UF Career Collab Career Development Hub UF GO Toolkit Profile Request Travel Expense Approvals Mobile Leadership Development Toolkit Faculty Excellence and Advancement Organizational Development Employee Education Program Employee Education Program Policy EEP FAQs EEP Contacts and Other Resources Checklist for Students Attending UF Deadlines Getting Started Course Selection at UF Application Submission EEP Registration and Fee Liability EEP Refund Policy UF Students – EEP Application Submission Financial Obligations and Waiver Process Checklist for Students Attending Santa Fe Checklist for Students Who Work Outside of Alachua County Employee Awards Superior Accomplishment Awards About the Award How to Nominate SAA 2026 Winners SAA 2025 Winners Promotion Toolkit Florida Government Productivity Awards Service Recognition Program Service Recognition Award Recipients 2026 Service Recognition Liaisons Meritorious Service Awards President’s Medallion University Medallion Tenure and Promotion Gator Business Administrator Services New Business Admin Onboarding GBAS Certification GBAS Community of Practice GBAS History & Team Career Development Hub Working at UF Employee Handbook Employment Status Career Path Leaving UF UF Engaged Toolkit Job Classifications Employment Verifications & Records Compensation and Payroll Salary Structure and Pay Grades Paycheck Information Direct Deposit Tax Pay Adjustments Understanding Overtime W-2 Information Teams Titles Policies and Guidelines Public Records Requests Policies and Procedures Immigration Compliance – Travel Information Harassment Prevention Employee Relations Helping Employees In Distress Report an Issue Harassment and Discrimination Employee Disability Accommodations Workers’ Compensation Union Information UF Engaged Toolkit Disciplinary Processes Employee Handbook Services For Employees Parking Child Care Travel Ergonomics Housing Wellness UF Dual Career Program Veteran Time Tracking myUFL About UF Campus Information Events News myUFL Updating Emergency Contact Keeping Your Address Up-to-Date Name Changes Education Updates myUFL Basics Contacts Contact Us Office of the Vice President Staff Directory University Benefits, Retirement & Leave Strategic Initiatives Employee Relations Contact Employee Relations Classification & Compensation Employment Operations & Records Talent Acquisition & Onboarding Training & Organizational Development Communications & Worklife Branding, Identity and ADA Resources Design & Branding Requests Strategy & Copywriting Requests Organizational Chart Emergency Guidance Public Records Requests HR Liaisons Report an Issue Employee Inquiry and Complaint Procedures Submitting a Formal Complaint Employee Relations Complaint Form We can’t wait to see what you do here! At UF, we encourage career exploration, development, and success. The Career Development Hub is designed to help employees manage and navigate their career paths at UF. This page provides resources developed to foster continuous learning, personal growth, and professional advancement. Career Development Navigator Our tailored microlearning experience offers you a look at the invaluable resources designed to help you achieve your personal and professional goals. Experience Now Plan for Progress Envision the future… Where do you see yourself? The resources below will help you communicate your strengths effectively and find new areas of growth, assess potential titles that interest you and their accompanying responsibilities and qualifications, and make the most of your performance evaluations as a way of establishing professional goals and tracking your accomplishments. Competencies & Proficiency Tables List of all TEAMS Titles competencies, with individual pages containing competency definitions, behavior statements, interview questions, and associated TEAMS Titles. Job Families & Career Path Maps Information on job families at UF, including maps reflecting the common pathways for all staff positions within a job family. TEAMS Titles Classifications Information on job responsibilities, education and experience, and competencies for TEAMS titles, organized by job family. UF Engaged: Staff Resources As the university’s framework for staff performance conversations, UF Engaged is the perfect time to discuss career development with your manager.  Learn more about how to utilize UF Engaged to keep track of performance as well as plan for your professional growth. Explore New Skills Set aside time to work on specifics. The resources below feature popular courses, training series, toolkits, and the HR training calendar to find upcoming courses that will fit into your busy schedule. HR Training Calendar Listing and calendar view of on-going HR trainings (synchronous) and wellness events. Leadership Development Toolkit Outlines a framework for the knowledge, skills, and behaviors needed to be an excellent leader at UF. LinkedIn Learning Training platform for online skill-building education. Managing at UF A comprehensive training series designed to help managers or aspiring mangers develop the skills to lead effectively and build thriving teams. This certification includes a range of workshops designed with UF in mind. New Manager Toolkit From the very first day on the job, UFHR wants every new manager to establish a solid foundation for success. This New Manager Toolkit provides you with key resources to increase your self-awareness, set your team up for success, and effectively manage and lead. Professional Development Overview of popular courses and information on special training series developed by UFHR Training & Organizational Development, such as Pro3, Thrive@UF, RAFT, and Gators Together. Toolkit Resource Center Featuring a variety of training materials, including simulations, instruction guides and UFHR courses, toolkits offer just-in-time training for both business processes and professional development resources. Make a Move When preparation meets opportunity. The resources below feature tips, exercises, and important aspects to keep in mind as you invest time and energy into progressing your career. From cover letters and job postings to nailing your next interview, we have developed resources for you to feel equipped along the way. Before, During & After the Interview Tips and tricks for what to do before, during, and after an interview. Career Catalyst This training series delves into topics such as creating a career portfolio, mapping your value proposition, and more. Foundations of a Great Resume and Cover Letter On-demand webinar coaching individuals on writing a great resume and cover letter. How to Engage in a Job Search in Gainesville Navigating Careers at UF A guide to get the most from UF’s Careers at UF portal. Tailoring a Resume Successful resumes often have one thing in common: they are tailored to the job description! Learn how to stand out by tailoring your resume. Cultivate Personal Growth The quality of our life and the quality of our work are interdependent. Below are resources to help cultivate your personal growth so that you can be your best self, on the job and off. Employee Education Program Information on tuition assistance for full-time Academic Personnel and TEAMS employees. Worklife at UF A range of resources to help faculty and staff build greater health and well-being. Facilitate Employee Development Create an environment that encourages and nurtures employee growth. The resources below highlight key skills managers need to support others in their personal and professional growth. From Exit Interview to Stay Conversations Don’t let valuable talent slip through your fingers. By the time an employee tells you they are leaving, it is too late to start a conversation. Discover strategies that foster meaningful connections that make employees feel valued, heard, and driven to excel. Support and Motivate Your Employees With so much emphasis on employee retention, well-being, and engagement, how can leaders support their employees? This video features three inspiring leaders that have identified strategies and techniques to enhance communication with their employees and create opportunities for growth and development. Support Employee Engagement As leaders, we all want our employees to be fully engaged, productive, and motivated at work. To achieve this, employees must feel supported and valued. Leaders have a critical role in listening to employee concerns, sharing their successes, and creating opportunities for growth and development. UF Engaged: Leader Resources The UF Engaged check-in includes space to discuss career development with your employee.  This page contains resources to help managers make the most of UF Engaged as a time to discuss performance and support professional growth. Search Toolkits Page Contents Popular Topics Holidays Benefits Salary Structure and Pay Grades Health Benefits Contact Us Employee Education Program Professional Development Direct Deposit Benefits Eligibility Training Programs Retirement Plans UF GO Toolkit About UF About the University of Florida Our Research & Impact Learn about UF’s benefits Worklife Resources Connect 8am-5pm (352) 392-2477 humanresources@ad.ufl.edu 903 West University Avenue Gainesville, FL 32601 Facebook Instagram Threads Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Privacy Statement Google Analytics Privacy Policy Translate Text-Only Site Map Web Update Requests Copyright © 2026, University of Florida"
    },
    "https://translate.google.com/translate?sl=auto&tl=en&hl=en-US&u=https://jobs.ufl.edu&client=webapp": {
      "title": "Come for a job.Grow a career.Gain a community.",
      "description": "Careers - Come for a job. Grow a career. Gain a community. Skip to content Main Navigation Careers Benefits Benefits Plans Time-Away Perks & Support Community The University of Florida Working at UF Career Growth ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Paths Career Types Resources How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference Explore Jobs How can we help you? Come for a job. Grow a career. Gain a community. Join a vibrant community that’s healing coastlines, exploring space, curing diseases and imagining wonders. Search for: Faculty Positions Join a community of distinguished scholars and educators at the University of Florida, where your expertise will drive innovation, teaching and research excellence. Staff Positions Join our community of career professionals in a variety of roles across a range of fields such as accounting, IT, health care, and more. Other Opportunities Join us as a Graduate Assistant, Student Assistant, or Postdoctoral Associate. Exclusive perks and benefits that grow with you. A whole-person approach to your well-being. Benefits Plans View the University of Florida's robust benefits plans including comprehensive health care, vision, dental, retirement planning, and a variety of optional programs to support you at work and beyond. Time Away Explore UF's collection of generous leave policies including sick and vacation time, paid family leave, paid medical leave and other extended leave programs. Perks & Support Learn more about the wide variety of perks and support services including employee discounts, mental health services, legal programs, employee education initiatives and more. Grow together. Grow greater. People come to UF for the diversity of job opportunities. They stay because they can grow their careers and gain a community. As a University of Florida employee, you’ll gain access to the institution’s extensive resources, cutting-edge technologies and opportunities for professional development to advance your career and beyond. Grow With Us A culture of care, opportunity and excellence for all. Join us at a top-tier intellectual playground limited only by your imagination, dreams and ambition. Become a part of a dynamic environment full of community partnerships, research opportunities and outreach programs that aim to improve the lives of people across the state of Florida and beyond. UF Community Resources How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference Popular Topics How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Veterans’ Preference Benefits Plans Career Paths Perks & Support Career Types Time-Away Working at UF The University of Florida ﻿﻿Professional Development Career Growth About UF About the University of Florida Our Research & Impact Learn about UF’s benefits Worklife Resources Connect Talent Acquisition & Onboarding 8am-5pm (352) 392-2477 talent@hr.ufl.edu 903 West University Avenue Gainesville, FL 32601 Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Privacy Statement Google Analytics Privacy Policy Translate Text-Only Site Map Web Update Requests Copyright © 2026, University of Florida"
    },
